Read the complete paper, methods/supporting material and correction together. Follow backgrounds, contamination pathways, isotope quantities, measurement limits, controls and independent interpretation. Apply the reasoning to a small-product chemical claim, preserving actual protocol and uncertainty; a chemically plausible reaction is not proof that its measured product came from the proposed feed.

The publisher's bibliographic/version dates and correction were checked on 29 October 2026. Nature's full-page retrieval encountered an authentication redirect. The DTU-hosted file identifies itself as an accelerated article preview, which differs from the final version and later correction; do not silently treat them as interchangeable. Retain version and copyright notices. No file, instrument protocol media or dataset is bundled.

